# App layout

This repo is one tree. `main.ts` is the `serve()` callback and boots it.
Every page is a feature folder that exports a `Group` from `mod.ts` (`mod.tsx`
when the file contains JSX). Nested, page-local components live in that folder.
`/` is a pathless group in `home/mod.tsx`. One-offs such as `staticFile` stay
on `main.ts`.

## File names

Deno snake_case. Feature folders match the path (`docs/` for `/docs`).
Layout and middleware files are `{folder}_{role}`: `menu_layout.tsx`,
`menu_middleware.ts`. Nested `reviews/` uses `reviews_layout.tsx`. At the app
root: `root_layout.tsx`, `logger_middleware.ts`, `errors.tsx`. Client modules
are `*_client.ts` (`clock_client.ts`) and sit beside the file that registers
them. No `routes/` directory, no app `client/` folder, no `_` magic prefixes,
and no `*_route.tsx`.

`errors.tsx` holds the named `notFound`, `error`, and `fatal`
exports. Those are not routes. Root `notFound` / `error` live on the root
callback; a feature group's `notFound` / `error` live on that group's `mod.ts`.
`fatal` stays on `serve()` options.

Ordinary extra modules (`todos.ts`, later `db.ts`) sit beside the handlers.
No blessed view / service / DAL layer: extract `menu_service.ts` or a
component when needed. No `layouts/` or `middleware/` folders.

## Exports

A component that returns `Element` is PascalCase (`Home`, `RootLayout`,
`ErrorPage`). Middleware and per-method handlers are camelCase (`logger`,
`list`, `add`).

`mod.ts` is the controller for that group: `group()` plus handlers (inline or
named functions in the same file). No `*_route.tsx` and no `controller.ts`
inside a feature folder. Only the root table in `main.ts` imports Groups and
binds one-offs.

## Table

`main.ts` is the `serve()` callback. It binds imported Groups and any root
one-offs, then calls `serve`. It does not bind `route("/")`. Feature folders
import `group` from `dashi` at module scope and export the `Group`. The parent
drops that value into `routes`. Do not `import { group }` inside a bag
callback. Do not export `route()`.

Every page is a feature folder `Group`, including one-page features:

```ts
import { group } from "dashi";

export const menu = group("/menu", ({ route }) => ({
  layouts: [MenuLayout],
  routes: [route("/", { GET: Menu })],
}));
```

`group("/", …)` is illegal. `/` is a pathless group in `home/mod.tsx`:

```tsx
import { group } from "dashi";

export const home = group(({ route }) => ({
  routes: [route("/", { GET: Home })],
}));

function Home() {
  return <h1>dashi.run</h1>;
}
```

Pathless `group(({ route }) => …)` is a layout/middleware shell with no extra
prefix, still exported from a file. Nested folders are nested groups. A
pre-built `Group` types `ctx.params` from its own prefix; nested groups do
not read ancestor params they did not declare. Shared data goes on `ctx.state`.

`main.ts` is:

```ts
import { CacheStrategy, serve, staticFile } from "dashi";
import { RootLayout } from "./root_layout.tsx";
import { error, fatal, notFound } from "./errors.tsx";
import { home } from "./home/mod.tsx";

if (import.meta.main) {
  serve(({ route }) => ({
    layouts: [RootLayout],
    notFound,
    error,
    routes: [
      home,
      route("/static/:file", {
        GET: (ctx) =>
          staticFile(ctx, `${import.meta.dirname}/static`, ctx.params.file, {
            strategy: CacheStrategy.Immutable,
          }),
      }),
      route("/assets/:file", {
        GET: (ctx) =>
          staticFile(ctx, `${import.meta.dirname}/assets`, ctx.params.file, {
            strategy: CacheStrategy.Public,
            maxAge: 3600,
          }),
      }),
    ],
  }), { fatal });
}
```

Later pages (`docs/`, and so on) are prefixed groups in their own folders.

## Imports

App code imports from `dashi`. JSX types (`Element`, `HTMLAttributes`,
`DashiNode`, `JSX`) import from `dashi/jsx-runtime`. Browser APIs import
from `dashi/client`.
